---
name: pull-request
description: Use when committed and validated feature-branch work is ready for a PR into `{{ base_branch }}`.
model: haiku
effort: high
allowed-tools: Bash(git branch:*), Bash(git rev-parse:*), Bash(git status:*), Bash(git fetch origin {{ base_branch }}:*), Bash(git diff:*), Bash(git log:*), Bash(git push:*), Bash(gh pr list:*), Bash(gh pr create:*){% if agent_merges %}, Bash(gh pr checks:*), Bash(gh pr view:*), Bash(gh pr merge:*){% endif %}
---

## Branch context

- Current branch: !`git branch --show-current`
- Upstream: !`git rev-parse --abbrev-ref --symbolic-full-name @{u} 2>/dev/null || echo "(none)"`
- Working tree: !`git status --short`
- Commits vs {{ base_branch }}: !`git fetch origin {{ base_branch }} --quiet 2>/dev/null; git --no-pager log origin/{{ base_branch }}..HEAD --oneline 2>/dev/null`
- Diff stat vs {{ base_branch }}: !`git --no-pager diff origin/{{ base_branch }}...HEAD --stat 2>/dev/null`

## Your task

1. Stop on `develop`, `staging`, or `main`; a dirty tree; or an empty diff from `origin/{{ base_branch }}`.
2. Require a current-session green `/gate` result for the current tree fingerprint. Stop if absent.
3. Return any open PR with the same head and base instead of creating a duplicate.
4. Push with `git push -u origin HEAD` unless the upstream is already
   `origin/<current-branch>`; new worktrees initially track their base, `origin/{{ base_branch }}`.
5. Read `git diff origin/{{ base_branch }}...HEAD`, then run `gh pr create --base {{ base_branch }}` with an imperative
   title (≤72 characters) and `Summary`, `Changes`, and `Test plan` sections. State that `/gate`
   passes. When the branch is named `<type>/<n>-<slug>`, add `Closes {{ issues_repo }}#<n>`: task
   issues live in that repo.
{%- if agent_merges %}
6. This project lets the agent merge its own PR into `{{ base_branch }}` (`agent_merges`). Wait for its
   checks with `gh pr checks <n> --watch`; on a failed or cancelled check, stop and report it. When
   every check has passed, read the head they ran on, `gh pr view <n> --json headRefOid --jq
   .headRefOid`, and merge that head only: `gh pr merge <n> --squash --match-head-commit <sha>`.
   The guard blocks the merge unless the PR is this repository's, the merge is a squash pinned to
   the current head, and every check on it has passed with `gate` among them.
7. Return the PR URL and the merge result.
{%- else %}
6. Return the PR URL.
{%- endif %}
